WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.235
"I wish Little Spot had turned out to be the thief after all," Maggie said with a sigh.

2
00:00:08.236 --> 00:00:11.635
"Then the mystery would be solved.

3
00:00:11.636 --> 00:00:16.379
And I wouldn't still be worried that Mom and Dad are going to make me stop riding."

4
00:00:16.380 --> 00:00:22.345
Henry, Cole, and Maggie were at the lemonade stand talking about what had happened yesterday.

5
00:00:22.346 --> 00:00:26.500
"We thought Little Spot was guilty at first," Cole said.

6
00:00:26.501 --> 00:00:29.912
"But then Henry started thinking logically again."

7
00:00:29.913 --> 00:00:36.495
Henry smiled. "Little Spot did grab your sandal," he reminded Maggie.

8
00:00:36.496 --> 00:00:39.099
"But then I thought of something.

9
00:00:39.100 --> 00:00:42.955
Why would a dog steal things only from you?

10
00:00:42.956 --> 00:00:49.378
It didn't make sense. The other riders leave their stuff sitting around too."

11
00:00:49.379 --> 00:00:54.078
"That's why we questioned everyone after your lesson," Cole went on.

12
00:00:54.079 --> 00:00:58.329
"We wanted to make sure the thief wasn't stealing stuff from everyone."

13
00:00:58.330 --> 00:01:05.239
"Nobody else is missing anything," Henry said. "Well, except for Ms. Wood."

14
00:01:05.240 --> 00:01:11.015
Cole nodded. "She said the barn cat's bed has been missing for a few days.

15
00:01:11.016 --> 00:01:13.934
But she's pretty sure a raccoon took that."

16
00:01:13.935 --> 00:01:20.443
"We also did an experiment to see if Little Spot would try to grab anything else," Henry said.

17
00:01:20.444 --> 00:01:26.497
"We used Cole's sock. Little Spot sniffed it, but he didn't pick it up."

18
00:01:26.498 --> 00:01:31.955
"So we decided that Little Spot just likes to grab shoes," Cole said.

19
00:01:31.956 --> 00:01:37.222
"My neighbor's dog is the same way, except he only steals TV remote controls."

20
00:01:37.223 --> 00:01:44.570
Maggie sighed again. "Well, it definitely wasn't Big Spot either," she said.

21
00:01:44.571 --> 00:01:47.361
"He might have been able to grab my sock.

22
00:01:47.362 --> 00:01:50.202
But he couldn't have taken my bracelet.

23
00:01:50.203 --> 00:01:55.909
I put it in my bag as I led him out, and it was missing as soon as I got back."

24
00:01:55.910 --> 00:02:03.021
"Really? Then I guess we can rule out all of the animal suspects," Henry said.

25
00:02:03.022 --> 00:02:09.619
Cole laughed. "Yeah. The barn cat couldn't have picked up your grooming brush."

26
00:02:09.620 --> 00:02:13.841
"So who are our human suspects?" Maggie asked.

27
00:02:13.842 --> 00:02:19.830
"All the other riders in your class," Henry said. "Plus Jill."

28
00:02:19.831 --> 00:02:22.231
"Right," Cole said.

29
00:02:22.232 --> 00:02:26.423
"We found out that Jill wishes she had more money for riding.

30
00:02:26.424 --> 00:02:30.048
What if she stole your stuff so she could sell it?"

31
00:02:30.049 --> 00:02:34.213
"Who would buy one sock?" Maggie asked.

32
00:02:34.214 --> 00:02:36.991
"Nobody," Henry answered.

33
00:02:36.992 --> 00:02:41.415
"We figured you might have lost that on your way into the barn."

34
00:02:41.416 --> 00:02:49.019
Maggie frowned. "You're as bad as my parents! I didn't lose that sock.

35
00:02:49.020 --> 00:02:52.906
I know it was in my bag when I put the bag down!"

36
00:02:52.907 --> 00:02:55.195
Henry wasn't so sure.

37
00:02:55.196 --> 00:03:00.209
He still didn't think Maggie was careless enough to lose the check or the other stuff.

38
00:03:00.210 --> 00:03:07.599
But it would be easy for her to drop a sock without noticing, especially when she was excited about going riding.

39
00:03:07.600 --> 00:03:12.690
He didn't say that though. He didn't want to make Maggie angry.

40
00:03:12.691 --> 00:03:17.072
"How well do you know Eleanor?" he asked instead.

41
00:03:17.073 --> 00:03:20.135
"Not that well." Maggie shrugged.

42
00:03:20.136 --> 00:03:25.542
"We've only had four lessons together. But I doubt she's the thief."

43
00:03:25.543 --> 00:03:30.873
"Why?" Cole asked. "You just said you don't know her very well.

44
00:03:30.874 --> 00:03:33.819
How do you know she's not sneaky?"

45
00:03:33.820 --> 00:03:38.245
"Because she takes such good care of her dog," Maggie said.

46
00:03:38.246 --> 00:03:42.907
"She's just as crazy about Little Spot as I am about my kittens.

47
00:03:42.908 --> 00:03:46.163
Someone like that has to be a good person."

48
00:03:46.164 --> 00:03:51.107
"Okay," Henry said. "But what about the others?

49
00:03:51.108 --> 00:03:55.217
We noticed Daisy was acting kind of competitive."

50
00:03:55.218 --> 00:04:00.511
"Yeah, she's always like that." Maggie rolled her eyes.

51
00:04:00.512 --> 00:04:03.297
"She wants to try everything first.

52
00:04:03.298 --> 00:04:06.344
And she thinks she's the best at whatever we do."

53
00:04:06.345 --> 00:04:12.431
"Then there's Zach," Cole said. "He was complaining about everything.

54
00:04:12.432 --> 00:04:15.803
What if he's stealing stuff because he hates riding?"

55
00:04:15.804 --> 00:04:20.674
"I still think his sister, Jill, is a better suspect," Henry said.

56
00:04:20.675 --> 00:04:25.325
"She has the best motive. She needs money."

57
00:04:25.326 --> 00:04:29.923
"I agree, Henry. But here come some customers."

58
00:04:29.924 --> 00:04:34.080
Maggie pointed to several people heading toward the lemonade stand.

59
00:04:34.081 --> 00:04:37.116
"We'll have to finish talking about this later."

60
00:04:37.117 --> 00:04:41.109
"I hope we can solve the mystery today," Maggie said.

61
00:04:41.110 --> 00:04:45.749
"Otherwise Mom said this might be my last lesson for a while."

62
00:04:45.750 --> 00:04:52.546
She sounded upset. Henry didn't blame her.

63
00:04:52.547 --> 00:04:57.333
It was a few days later, and The Lemonade Detectives were back at the barn.

64
00:04:57.334 --> 00:05:01.203
"Do you have both of your socks today?" Cole asked.

65
00:05:01.204 --> 00:05:03.959
Maggie made a face at him.

66
00:05:03.960 --> 00:05:08.582
"You already asked me that twenty times," she said.

67
00:05:08.583 --> 00:05:12.114
"I told you, I stuck them in my boots today.

68
00:05:12.115 --> 00:05:14.887
There's no way they can fall out."

69
00:05:14.888 --> 00:05:18.231
Henry noticed Ms. Wood hurrying toward them.

70
00:05:18.232 --> 00:05:21.939
The barn owner had an anxious expression on her face.

71
00:05:21.940 --> 00:05:25.190
"Maggie!" Ms. Wood said.

72
00:05:25.191 --> 00:05:29.998
"There you are. I need to speak with you about something serious."

73
00:05:29.999 --> 00:05:33.500
"I'm not late, am I?" Maggie asked.

74
00:05:33.501 --> 00:05:40.420
Ms. Wood shook her head. "It's not that," she said. "We have a problem.

75
00:05:40.421 --> 00:05:50.208
Right after you left the barn the other day, I realized something: Big Spot's saddle pad is missing!"

